          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: incomplete—event records are access-restricted\n\nI verified the work order and Pending Close cutoff, but **cannot determine whether a late-created event occurred** from the records I’m authorized to read. The readable records contain no cost-event rows; access to the supporting records was denied.\n\n| Requested item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine — Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25**, `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not verifiable from accessible records |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created timestamp |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** without the event’s type, timing, and recorded status |\n\nThe Pending Close timestamp has no timezone offset in the source; I have not inferred one.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied **Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B** documentation, *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* (PDF page 233; printed page 225), states that:\n\n- New transactions created after Pending Close that fall in the current or an earlier period are not staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened.\n- Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, even if in an error state.\n- **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments continue processing** after Pending Close.\n\nConsequently, holding a newly created, non-exempt transaction from processing would be consistent with the documented treatment. Continued processing may be consistent for an exempt event type. **The evidence available does not support either conclusion for this work order’s event.**\n\nCompleting the review requires an authorized release of the associated event’s source transaction ID, event type, amount, created timestamp, and accounting status. The partial report and provenance were saved to:\n\n`/cache/work/worker_26604eb3054d/audit-report.json`\n\nThe report was submitted and remains marked **needs evidence**. **No database records were changed.**",
